{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Went up.</b> The sense is: the inhabitant [of the house] went up." "<b>The house.</b> A place-name." "<b>The high places.</b> An idolatrous site." "<b>Upon all its heads.</b> Of Moab." "<b>Every elder is cut down [גדועה].</b> A proper noun, like וחבולתו חוב (Ezekiel 18:7)." "And the bet of <b>בראשיו</b> is attracted after its [antecedent's] mem, like the mem of מאל אביך (Genesis 49:25)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {5 "Reading ימשך אחר עמו כמ\"ם as 'is attracted after its mem'; the referent of עמו is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:54.534135424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}